 "text": "Hello, how are things going? In most places, you can boil it away, treat it or bury it on designated spot. Which do you prefer? Even with eco soap, boiling is fastest and leaves no smell. You can, but dig a little deeper than you would a typical camp spot, so there's no risk of contamination. Campsites want keep things clean and easy to manage, so they' fairly standard. Which method are you leaning towards? Good camper. Just remember, if you' unsure, ask a ranger, they're used people asking.",
